From 3573f8a6a49870956a4a9541325fe866c125cabf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: greyoak111 <151205158+greyoak111@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 16:20:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 32/49] Add on-device live captions
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A Captions tab in the dock turns on live captions for one OBS audio
source (the microphone by default) in Mandarin, Taiwanese Mandarin,
Cantonese or English. Speech is recognized on the Mac with Apple's
SpeechAnalyzer (macOS 26+); nothing is uploaded. A new "LiveHime
captions" source shows the words on stream, bottom-aligned, keeping the
latest words that fit and clearing a few seconds after speech stops.

The recognizer's spacing around Chinese is removed and homophones such
as 直播机 are corrected to 直播姬. When audio stops arriving, silence is
fed so the last sentence still finishes. Works without signing in.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
